`dfs2` starts from all `st=2` nodes on the *reversed* graph and marks nodes that can reach `st=2` (incrementing `ans`).
A node gets `ans=2` if it satisfies both conditions.
Note: `dfs2` stops if it hits a node with `st=1`. `dfs1` has a commented-out stop for `st=2`.

